WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.290
Traveling the world with a stranger, dead
rats, and the jazz routine from hell — we're

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:09.159
pretty sure these endings didn't seem so disturbing
in the theater.

00:00:09.159 --> 00:00:16.839
John Woo's 1997 action flick Face/Off circles
around two characters who face off with their,

00:00:16.839 --> 00:00:18.279
well, faces off.

00:00:18.279 --> 00:00:24.569
FBI agent Sean Archer holds a personal vendetta
against Castor Troy, a psychopathic bomber

00:00:24.569 --> 00:00:26.859
who murdered Archer's 6-year-old son.

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:32.220
Archer's vendetta drives him to take extreme
measures to capture Troy and foil his plans,

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:37.713
eventually leading him to undergo a temporary
surgery that makes him look and sound like Troy.

00:00:37.713 --> 00:00:43.329
However, a string of unfortunate events confines
Archer in the prison he was infiltrating as

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:47.940
Troy, allowing the real Troy to adopt Archer's
face and identity.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:53.250
As a result, Archer's wife, Eve, goes through
a series of traumas at the film's climax.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:57.809
She first finds out that she's been living
with a sociopathic killer who she'd mistaken

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:02.785
for her husband, and then she is held hostage
by Troy — who still has Sean's face, by the way.

00:01:02.785 --> 00:01:06.230
After that, their daughter, Jamie, is also
taken hostage by Troy.

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:10.330
In the end, Sean wins back his face and reunites
with his family.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:15.580
In reality, however, it wouldn't be easy for
Eve and Jamie to immediately "unsee" Sean

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:18.910
as the murderer and sociopath that Troy was.

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:22.830
Basically, that family is going to need a
whole lot of therapy.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:28.570
Whiplash tells the tale of an extremely toxic
teacher-student pair who go to extreme lengths

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:32.360
to perfect their craft and musical talents
— at the expense of their relationships,

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.010
family, and their own mental health.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:40.200
Throughout the film, ambitious drummer Andrew
Neiman relentlessly hammers towards his desire

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.889
for greatness, fueled by his abrasive music
teacher Terence Fletcher.

00:01:44.889 --> 00:01:47.560
"Why do you suppose I just hurled a chair
at your head, Neiman?"

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:50.300
"I don't know."

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:50.857
"Sure you do."

00:01:51.556 --> 00:01:52.556
"... the tempo?"

00:01:52.726 --> 00:01:57.430
As a result, Andrew distances himself from
his father, splits up with his girlfriend,

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:02.600
repeatedly injures his hands from overplaying,
and is involved in a near-fatal car accident

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.680
before making his way to a concert.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:09.920
The climactic concert sequence, in which Andrew
finally earns Fletcher's nod of approval following

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:14.260
a rigorous drum solo, gives the impression
of a triumphant ending for Andrew.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:19.310
But with time, viewers might come to see that
Andrew has ultimately fallen into a deep pit

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:21.187
of suffering and self-abuse.

00:02:21.187 --> 00:02:26.390
Andrew's very likely dark path after the film's
events is hinted at by Fletcher's constant

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:31.620
idolization of jazz musician Charlie Parker,
who himself suffered from mental health issues

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:34.966
and drug addictions, and who died at age 34.

00:02:35.137 --> 00:02:40.780
In Robert Zemeckis' classic film Forrest Gump,
the titular character's many adventures take

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.200
him all around the world.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:47.220
Despite his low IQ, Forrest achieves fame
on the football field, fights in Vietnam,

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:51.540
plays ping-pong against the Chinese, receives
the Medal of Honor from President Lyndon B.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:56.580
Johnson, and reports an office burglary that
unfolds into the Watergate scandal.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:01.490
Plus, he finds himself crossing paths with
the likes of Elvis Presley and John Lennon.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.790
However, it's Forrest's relationship with
his childhood sweetheart, Jenny, that serves

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.030
as the film's unifying narrative thread.

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:12.090
When Forrest finally catches up to Jenny at
the end of the movie, she reveals that she's

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:17.240
been infected with an "unknown virus" and
that she has a son who is also named "Forrest."

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:22.700
Jenny succumbs to her illness, which is implied
to be HIV/AIDS, leaving Forrest Jr. in the

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:28.460
care of Forrest Sr. Tragically, since HIV/AIDS
can be transmitted from mother to child during

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:32.350
pregnancy, it's possible that Forrest Jr.
also carries the virus.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:37.970
In a 2019 interview with Yahoo! Entertainment,
Forrest Gump screenwriter Eric Roth confirmed

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:43.010
that the now-shelved sequel would have begun
with Forrest Jr. being diagnosed with AIDS,

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:46.280
facing bullying and discrimination in school
as a result.

00:03:46.364 --> 00:03:52.280
In 50 First Dates, Drew Barrymore's Lucy struggles
with a form of anterograde amnesia after an

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:55.940
accident, preventing her from being able to
create any memories.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:04:00.550
Each day is a "reset" for Lucy, who always
believes that it's October 13th, the date

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:01.840
of her injury.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:06.150
Lucy's brother and father go to considerable
efforts to recreate the same event for her

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:11.750
every day with the help of the owners of a
local cafe — which is where she meets Adam Sandler's Henry.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:16.299
Henry falls in love with Lucy and devises
a way to help her to move on to the next day,

00:04:16.299 --> 00:04:20.769
by making her watch a "recap" film of her
life up until the moment she wakes up.

00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:25.099
Although the ending seems perfectly wholesome
and heartening, the implications are more

00:04:25.099 --> 00:04:27.569
distressing when you really think about them.

00:04:27.569 --> 00:04:31.210
Lucy — who is revealed to have a child with
Henry at the end of the film — would have

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:36.280
had to wake up every single day for nine months
not knowing she was pregnant, let alone waking

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.080
up on a boat beside a stranger.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:42.930
Not to mention the fact that Henry is going
to have to spend most of his life painstakingly

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:45.900
editing and updating her "recap" videos.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:48.176
It's not exactly ideal.

00:04:48.176 --> 00:04:53.520
The plot of Toy Story culminates with Woody
and Buzz joining forces with Sid's mistreated

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:57.150
and disfigured toys in order to teach the
human bully a lesson.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:01.779
As Sid is about to send Buzz flying into the
air using a firework, Woody speaks to Sid

00:05:01.779 --> 00:05:07.334
directly through his pre-programmed voice
box — seriously deviating from his usual lines.

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:10.565
"Who are you calling busted, buster?

00:05:10.565 --> 00:05:15.386
That's right, I'm talking to you… Sid Phillips."

00:05:15.386 --> 00:05:21.029
This acts as a cue for Sid's toys to crawl
up to him slowly in creepy, Night of the Living

00:05:21.029 --> 00:05:23.449
Dead fashion, heightening Sid's horror.

00:05:23.449 --> 00:05:28.542
The scene reaches its apex when Woody bursts
out from his "toy" form and tells Sid:

00:05:28.542 --> 00:05:33.540
"So play nice."

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:38.249
Sid screams and runs away as the toys rejoice
in their newfound freedom.

00:05:38.249 --> 00:05:39.479
Great, right?

00:05:39.479 --> 00:05:45.180
Well, while Sid getting his long-overdue comeuppance
seems fitting for a kids' movie, adults will

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:49.949
notice that Sid now has to live with the guilt
of having tortured living things.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:55.889
Since toys are constantly present in our culture,
existing in nearly every home and retail establishment,

00:05:55.889 --> 00:06:00.159
seeing a seemingly innocent little toy will
most likely trigger painful reminders for

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:03.550
him — reminders that these things are actually
sentient.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:07.759
What makes it worse is that Sid can't talk
to anyone about it, since no one would ever

00:06:07.759 --> 00:06:08.759
believe him.

00:06:08.759 --> 00:06:13.490
It's a pretty cruel fate, especially considering
he never thought he was hurting anyone in

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:15.000
the first place.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:20.550
Big follows 12-year-old Josh Baskin, a boy
whose wish to grow "big" comes true when he

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:22.979
grows into an adult body overnight.

00:06:22.979 --> 00:06:27.460
Since his mother doesn't believe that this
30-year-old man is indeed her son, Josh moves

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:32.379
to New York City and gets an entry level job
at a prominent toy manufacturing company.

00:06:32.379 --> 00:06:37.279
That's where he impresses owner Mr. MacMillan
with his insight into current toys and his

00:06:37.279 --> 00:06:38.370
childlike enthusiasm.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:41.789
Soon, Josh is promoted to vice president of
product development.

00:06:41.789 --> 00:06:47.500
Along the way, Josh develops a romantic relationship
with co-worker Susan Lawrence, which fades

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:51.380
away as our protagonist finds adulthood more
and more exhausting.

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:53.520
Eventually, he wishes to become a child again.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:58.199
Despite Susan's initial disbelief, she is
ultimately convinced that Josh is a child,

00:06:58.199 --> 00:07:02.759
and she bids a tearful goodbye at the end
of the film as she drops him at his home.

00:07:02.759 --> 00:07:07.199
Worryingly, the revelation that Josh was a
12-year-old child all along doesn't cause

00:07:07.199 --> 00:07:12.360
Susan any distress at any time during the
movie's ending — which is especially odd

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:15.349
considering that she had previously spent
the night at Josh's apartment.

00:07:15.349 --> 00:07:20.009
The fact that she still harbors love for Josh
at the end of the film, as well as her total

00:07:20.009 --> 00:07:26.234
lack of regret over having been intimate with
him, indicate something seriously wrong with Susan.

00:07:26.234 --> 00:07:31.059
Ratatouille is the tale of Remy the rat, the
only rodent among his clan with a taste for

00:07:31.059 --> 00:07:32.059
good food.

00:07:32.059 --> 00:07:37.189
A series of events causes Remy to become separated
from his family, and the ambitious rat finds

00:07:37.189 --> 00:07:42.569
himself in Paris, home to Gusteau's, the restaurant
of Remy's cooking idol Auguste Gusteau.

00:07:42.569 --> 00:07:48.360
Here, he befriends the clumsy but sweet Alfredo
Linguini, who Remy uses as a human conduit

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.229
to channel his culinary talents.

00:07:50.229 --> 00:07:56.929
Eventually, Gusteau's regains its lost reputation
and opens the door to Remy's own bistro, La Ratatouille.

00:07:56.929 --> 00:08:02.339
Granted, a rat becoming a chef is an amusing
premise for a Pixar movie, but perhaps not

00:08:02.339 --> 00:08:03.639
so much for real life.

00:08:03.639 --> 00:08:08.520
Given that the average lifespan of a rat is
2 years — and Remy seems to be well into

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:12.990
his adulthood — it's very likely that Remy
will pass away less than a year after the

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:14.279
film's ending.

00:08:14.279 --> 00:08:19.659
Since his newly opened bistro La Ratatouille
hinges on his culinary prowess, it's not exactly

00:08:19.659 --> 00:08:25.150
ideal for the bistro's management and investors
that its head chef won't live past a year.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:29.669
Then again, we're talking about a rat that
can cook, understand English, and control

00:08:29.669 --> 00:08:32.659
a human being like a puppet by pulling on
his hair.

00:08:32.659 --> 00:08:38.500
Maybe we can give Pixar the benefit of the
doubt and assume rats live longer in the Ratatouille universe.

00:08:38.706 --> 00:08:45.620
At the end of Back to the Future, Marty McFly
returns from 1955 to an altered 1985 where

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:48.709
his family's personalities have done a complete
180.

00:08:48.709 --> 00:08:52.790
His father seems to be much more confident
and has built a successful writing career,

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:57.089
his mother seems healthy and happy in her
marriage, his brother has a well-paying job,

00:08:57.089 --> 00:08:59.431
and his sister has quite the active dating
life.

00:08:59.431 --> 00:09:01.081
"Great Scott!"

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:05.820
On the surface, this seems like the best possible
future for anyone to return to.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:10.661
However, because Marty still remembers events
from the earlier timeline, his "new" family

00:09:10.661 --> 00:09:12.769
members are total strangers to him.

00:09:12.769 --> 00:09:16.670
This means that he'll have to deal with the
knowledge of his parents' prior personalities

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:18.940
without being able to discuss it with anybody.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:24.110
It's also unsettling to consider that, if
Marty perhaps created a new timeline, his

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:28.090
parents in the original timeline may still
be waiting for him to return — if they haven't

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:29.860
been written out of time entirely.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:34.890
Additionally, the family now employs Biff
as a valet, seemingly forgetting that 30 years

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:39.730
ago, on the night of the prom dance, Biff
tried to force himself onto Lorraine, forcing

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:41.630
George to come to the rescue.

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:45.050
That can't be the most comfortable situation
for poor Lorraine.

